WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.968
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:10.224 --> 00:00:12.390
SPEAKER 1: Everybody, no
matter where you come from,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.540
has someone that
they care about.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.940
We built an app that is
a peer-to-peer safety

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.910
network that allows people
to select companions

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.560
from their contact book to
watch them walk home safely.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.740
And if they ever feel
nervous or unsafe,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.070
they can notify you
within three taps.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:38.130
When we chose Google Maps for
the foundation of our app,

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.120
it was something that
developers trusted,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.080
but the consumer also trusted.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.620
We want to build something that
changes the way people live

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.757
and improves their life.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.300
SPEAKER 2: Methane is
a huge global threat

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.850
to all of our ecosystems
and our health.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:59.832
It affects everything
we are and we do.

00:00:59.832 --> 00:01:01.540
And so I feel really
compelled day to day

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.110
to get up and try to fix
the problem in the best,

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.496
most impactful way that I can.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.780
What we've done is
put methane sensors

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.930
on a number of Street View
cars to map and measure methane

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.732
levels coming from
under city streets.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.450
The maps that we've created,
with the help of the API,

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.050
have really made this
data visible in a way

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.520
that it's never been before.

00:01:36.004 --> 00:01:37.420
SPEAKER 3: There's
nothing getting

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.628
you ready for being homeless.

00:01:38.628 --> 00:01:40.870
All of a sudden, everything
that we take for granted

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.190
is taken away.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:46.080
And we find ourselves basically
sleeping in the streets.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.803
I think it's my duty, as
a person that's actually

00:01:48.803 --> 00:01:52.810
lived the experience, to give
back and actually help others.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.420
SPEAKER 4: In Australia, one
in 200 people are homeless,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.500
but 80% of them have got
a smartphone of some kind.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.980
So there's a
tremendous opportunity

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.390
to get information
into their hands.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.230
The whole point
of our application

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:08.320
is to help our users find
their way to the services

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.250
that they need.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.350
Using the Google Maps
API means that we

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:18.317
can give people the information
they need to make a decision.

00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:19.900
SPEAKER 3: There's
no signpost saying,

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.620
this is where you get food,
this is where you get blankets.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.370
It doesn't happen.

00:02:25.571 --> 00:02:27.070
We're giving this
for somebody who's

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.310
still homeless to actually help
them to come forward and be

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:31.510
reconnected.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.860
[MUSIC PLAYING]

